Man I did some stupid shit. Let this be a record of what NOT to do:

- I played an elf (Wiz). I had no idea elves only go up to Str 18, Con
16. Can't. Carry. Shit. Not worth the boost to Int and Wis IMO

- /oC went right into my BoH just as I was getting ready for Gehennom.
Goodbye all my scrolls, all my rings, all my gems, most of my good
wands, all my potions except 20 potions of holy water, my magic
marker, and 75K in coins. I almost quit. However, I stashed my spell
books in a chest and remembered another BoH from Mine's End (and had
the holy water from before). I pressed on.

- Killing co-aligned priests (and maybe the priest in the Valley of
Death?) zaps your protection. Oops! I just wanted spell books. Bah. I
think my base AC was 9 upon ascending. Because of this and the /oC
event, my final AC was just -15. Wiz + HP of 434 so not a huge deal.

- Apparently you can't make unholy water by praying at the altar in
the Valley of Death. Who knew! Good thing I had disintegration
resistance, but this cost me all my body armor. The rational was that
I didn't have reflection for much of Gehennom (simply not in the
game). I FINALLY found my ?oG in Orcus Town but lacked unholy water to
curse it and send in the silver dragons. I finally got it via blessed ?
oRC while confused.

- I neglected wands once I had all my spells (e.g. no /oT). I
completely forgot "oY messes you up spell casting-wise. As such the
planes were quite scary (survived on Conflict and Charm Monster) and I
was woefully unprepared for the Astral Plane. I made it to the first
altar on my own, but then an Archon showed up and summoned baddies
every other turn. It wasn't until he summoned a cockatrice that it
became trivial. That rubber chicken really saved me in the end. 3rd
altar was the winner.

- No +oID and only once did reading a scroll ID my entire inventory.
This didn't stop me from getting amnesia several times by run ins with
mind flayers.

- I entered the Astral Plane with conflict. Ugh.

I haven't played for years and I played this to prove to my friend I
don't completely suck at the game, but apparently I do. He doesn't
like the fact that I 1. stay Burdened for most of the game until I
have most of my ascension kit and 2. murder human shopkeepers when
playing neutral humans (amongst other things).

Coolest thing ever: I killed Jubilex at xp level 6 or 7 by 1.
summoning him by sacrificing an elf, 2. going blind, 3. accidentally
making him angry, 4. casting MM while swallowed, and 5. using my
unicorn horn to cure myself in one shot :)

Overall worth it. The conduct challenges made the end game more
difficult (or at least less easy). For example I didn't have
reflection when black dragons started showing up, so I had to be very
careful my first encounter. And I didn't get any worthwhile armor
until Gehennom. Found my speed boots on the last level. Also, I didn't
have mapping for Gehennom. I would cast clairvoyance and detect
treasure then teleport to objects and recast clairvoyance to find the
staircase. The early game was easier than playing a Tourist, but the
end game was a good bit harder.

It took me 7 tries. 4 Valks and 3 Wizards I think. Half of those were
me quitting in Mine town when there wasn't a BoH in Sokoban or there.

5,236,078 points after 59,584 moves brizna-Wiz-Elf-Mal-Cha. Yahoo!


